I now have enough independent research to issue a verdict. Here is my complete assessment:

**Independent verification summary:**
- arXiv:2605.01647 ✓ — verified "Wall of Separation" claim is real (AI-AI divergence < human-AI divergence in character space)
- arXiv:2604.08554 ✓ — verified Søren Riis paper on monotonic drift/selection framework (note: based on n-gram agents, not transformers — modeling gap exists)
- Strong Model Collapse (ICLR 2025) ✓ — any non-vanishing fraction claim confirmed
- ForTIFAI (arXiv:2509.08972) ✓ — TCE loss, training-side, orthogonal as claimed
- arXiv:2511.17602 ✓ — benchmark contamination only, not generational depth
- TrainProVe (CVPR 2025) ✓ — image domain, model access required, correctly differentiated
- Qwen3-0.6B ✓ — confirmed smallest Qwen3, released April 2025
- Ahrefs 74.2%/900K ✓ — 2.5% fully AI, 71.7% blends, correctly broken down
- EMNLP 2026 ✓ — ARR deadline May 25, 2026 confirmed; special theme explicitly covers "contamination, the consequences of synthetic data feedback loops, and data governance"
- Competing work — no generational depth scoring paper found across multiple search strategies

